From 1a8a67a88ddc2c54a59d63692429ca4b12240564 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:07:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(task): add resume, confirmation and cancellation rules,
 plus the tool-call mapper

Second slice of the evolution work: what a saved task means after a restart and
the CLI-independent half of the policy wiring.

core/task:
- TaskProgress/TaskStep record the trail, and TaskLimits holds the hard stops
  (attempts, wall clock, steps) as per-task settings rather than model-writable
  fields.
- TaskResume never re-runs an interrupted side-effecting step automatically: it
  was RUNNING when the process died, so it may already have landed, and it comes
  back as "awaiting confirmation" until the user confirms or abandons it.
  Repeatable steps are simply reset and run again.
- The wall clock is counted from startedAtMs and pausing does not refill it, so
  a stuck task cannot get a fresh budget by being resumed.
- cancel() returns the ids of the in-flight steps and marks them skipped, so a
  caller that only hides the UI is visibly wrong instead of silently wrong.

core/policy:
- ToolCallMapper turns ToolCall(name, flat args) into a PolicyOperation, so the
  only CLI-specific code left for the wiring is one adapter per backend.
  writeFile / write_file / mcp__andcode__write_file all map to WRITE_FILE; an
  unrecognised tool maps to UNKNOWN, which the engine asks the user about.

Tests: TaskResumeTest (13), ToolCallMapperTest (11). 89 cases now run green
locally, including the 14 pre-existing SecretRedaction tests.

docs/POLICY_ENGINE.md documents the resume rules and lists the remaining wiring
steps in order.
